  "final_text": "I can't give you a reliable ending MRR from these two files. Here's what they contain and the closest figure I can give.\n\n**Why the revenue file can't be read as MRR**\n\n`monthly_revenue.csv` has `dt, segment, amount`, and April's amounts are negative in every segment (Enterprise −13,285, Mid-Market −3,080, SMB −3,595). A month's MRR can't be negative, so `amount` is almost certainly a monthly *change* in MRR, not the month's total. To turn changes into ending MRR you need the MRR at the start, and neither file has it:\n\n- The revenue file starts in January 2026. But `customer_master.csv` shows about 100 customers already active during 2025, so MRR going into 2026 wasn't zero.\n- `customer_master.csv` has no revenue or price fields at all. It only has segment, country, plan, status and a status date.\n\n**Closest available figure: change in MRR since 1 Jan 2026**\n\nThese are the monthly amounts added up from January onwards, by segment. They show how much MRR has moved since January, **not** ending MRR:\n\n| Month (Q2 2026) | Enterprise | Mid-Market | SMB | Total |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Apr 2026 | 42,465 | 21,295 | 12,130 | **75,890** |\n| May 2026 | 43,225 | 27,175 | 15,265 | **85,665** |\n| Jun 2026 | 64,455 | 43,960 | 19,815 | **128,230** |\n\nEnding MRR would be the 31 Dec 2025 MRR plus these figures.\n\n**One more thing that doesn't add up:** in April, the customer file shows 6 new customers (status N) and 3 cancellations (status C, IDs 21, 41, 100). Yet April's revenue change is −19,960. That's possible, for example if many customers downgraded, but it makes me less sure what `amount` actually measures.\n\n**To finish this I need one of:**\n1. MRR at 31 Dec 2025, by segment, which I'd add to the table above; or\n2. A note on what `amount` means, if it isn't a monthly change; or\n3. A subscription or invoice export with MRR per customer, so I can rebuild ending MRR from the customer list.\n\nI used your date of 1 July 2026, so the last complete quarter is Q2 (April to June). My system clock says 26 October 2026, which would make it Q3 instead, but the files only go up to June anyway.",
